<%# The DSFR card, written out rather than taken from `CardComponent`: that one
    puts the title in the heading it renders, where this card's heading is a
    wording the directories publish and wears their mark.

    The requirement names the card, and it is named whatever the directories
    answered afterwards — a requirement nobody serves is still one the procedure
    rests on. What stands under the rule is therefore what varies: the document
    and the button that asks for it, or the refusal that stands in for both.

    Everything is in the content, as the identity card has it, and the rule
    between the two halves is the `<hr>` that card draws: the DSFR footer pulls
    its own edge past the card's padding, so a rule on it would run wider than
    the wording above it. %>
<div class="<%= css_classes %>" id="<%= anchor %>" data-controller="demo-card">
  <%# The cross of an added card, in its top right corner. Its name is said in
      words to whoever cannot see the icon, which criterion 11.9 of the RGAA
      asks of a button whose label is one. Outside what an answer replaces, so
      no country chosen takes it away. %>
  <% if removable? %>
    <%= button_to removal_path, method: :delete, form: { class: 'requirement-card__remove', lang: 'en' },
          class: 'fr-btn fr-btn--tertiary-no-outline fr-btn--sm fr-icon-close-line',
          title: t('components.demo_requirement_card.remove') do %>
      <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.remove') %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="fr-card__body">
    <div class="fr-card__content">
      <%# The artwork the DSFR gives a document, at the height of the title and
          the line under it. Decorative: what it depicts is what the two lines
          beside it say. %>
      <div class="pictogram-row">
        <%= render PictogramComponent.new(name: 'document/document') %>

        <div class="pictogram-row__wording">
          <% if titled? %>
            <%# The requirement alone, and no sentence around it: the title is
                the directory's word and nothing of ours. %>
            <h3 class="fr-card__title fr-h5 fr-mb-1v">
              <%= render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: requirement_language)) { requirement } %>
            </h3>
          <% end %>

          <%# The member state the evidence is to come from, above what it
              changes. Choosing sends it at once, and only what the resolution
              produces is replaced: the list keeps the focus, and the region
              below announces the new resolution — a content update, not the
              change of context RGAA 7.4 forbids. Offered on a card nothing
              satisfies too, which would otherwise have no way out of the
              country that serves nothing. %>
          <% if countries %>
            <%= form_with url: country_path, method: :patch, class: 'requirement-card__country fr-my-2w',
                  html: { lang: 'en' } do |form| %>
              <div class="fr-select-group fr-mb-0" data-demo-card-target="countryGroup">
                <%= form.label :pays, t('components.demo_requirement_card.country_label'),
                      class: 'fr-label', for: country_field %>
                <%= form.select :pays, options_for_select(countries, country_code), {},
                      class: 'fr-select', id: country_field,
                      data: { demo_card_target: 'countrySelect', action: 'change->demo-card#choose',
                              demo_card_list_param: 'country' } %>
                <%# What the card says when the choice got no answer this
                    application wrote: the server cannot say that it could not
                    be reached, so the sentence is rendered here, hidden, and
                    the controller shows it. Outside what an answer replaces,
                    so no answer takes it away but the controller. %>
                <%= tag.p t('components.demo_requirement_card.unreachable_html',
                            reload: link_to(t('components.demo_requirement_card.reload'),
                                            helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)),
                          class: 'fr-error-text', id: failure_field, hidden: true,
                          data: { demo_card_target: 'countryFailure' } %>
              </div>
              <%# The one region announcing what either list changed: it is never
                  replaced, by either answer. %>
              <p class="fr-sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-demo-card-target="status"></p>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>

          <%# What the country answers above the rule, which a country chosen
              replaces: the list of the evidence types it publishes, where it
              publishes several — requirement 26 of chapter 1 §2 has the user
              select the type —; the country alone, in its box, on a card that
              follows a request and offers no list of countries; the sentence
              saying nothing satisfies the requirement there; or nothing. %>
          <div class="fr-card__desc" data-demo-card-target="top">
            <% if evidence_types %>
              <%# Choosing sends it at once, and only the foot of the card is
                  replaced: the list keeps the focus, and the region of the
                  form of countries — rendered whenever this list is —
                  announces what the foot now says. No type is chosen in the
                  user's place, so the list opens on a prompt until one is. %>
              <%= form_with url: evidence_type_path, method: :patch, class: 'requirement-card__evidence-type',
                    html: { lang: 'en' } do |form| %>
                <div class="fr-select-group fr-mb-0" data-demo-card-target="typeGroup">
                  <%= form.label :type, t('components.demo_requirement_card.evidence_type_label'),
                        class: 'fr-label', for: evidence_type_field, data: { demo_card_announced: true } %>
                  <%= form.select :type, options_for_select(evidence_types, evidence_type_uuid),
                        { prompt: (t('components.demo_requirement_card.evidence_type_prompt') unless evidence_type_uuid) },
                        class: 'fr-select', id: evidence_type_field,
                        data: { demo_card_target: 'typeSelect', action: 'change->demo-card#choose',
                                demo_card_list_param: 'type' } %>
                  <%# Rendered here and hidden, as the country's: the server
                      cannot say it could not be reached. %>
                  <%= tag.p t('components.demo_requirement_card.evidence_type_unreachable_html',
                              reload: link_to(t('components.demo_requirement_card.reload'),
                                              helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)),
                            class: 'fr-error-text', id: evidence_type_failure_field, hidden: true,
                            data: { demo_card_target: 'typeFailure' } %>
                </div>
              <% end %>
            <% elsif !countries %>
              <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced><%= render country_tag %></p>
            <% elsif unsatisfiable? %>
              <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
                <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.unsatisfiable_html', country: render(country_tag)) %>
              </p>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="fr-mt-3w">

      <div class="requirement-card__actions" data-demo-card-target="foot">
        <% if nameable? %>
          <p class="fr-mb-0" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
            <%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.from_html',
                  evidence_type: render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: evidence_type_language)) { evidence_type },
                  provider: render(DirectoryValueComponent.new(lang: provider_language)) { provider }) %>
          </p>

          <% if unspoken %>
            <%# A warning and not a sentence among others: the card names a
                provider and offers nothing to ask it. The DSFR alert carries
                its icon besides its colour, which RGAA 3.1 wants. %>
            <div class="fr-alert fr-alert--warning fr-alert--sm fr-mt-2w requirement-card__refusal" lang="en">
              <p><%= t('components.demo_requirement_card.unsupported_version', version: unspoken.number) %></p>
            </div>
          <% elsif askable? %>
            <%# The button that opens the exchange, and everything that becomes of
                it. This element persists and its contents are what an answer
                replaces: it holds the announced region, which would announce
                nothing were it swapped out with what it announces. %>
            <div class="demo-request fr-mt-2w" aria-live="polite" data-controller="demo-request"
              data-action="submit->demo-request#submit"
              data-demo-request-url-value="<%= zone_path %>">
              <%= render zone %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        <%# A type still to choose offers no button and no refusal: requirement
            27 of chapter 1 §2 has the type and the provider named before any
            request is made, and nothing is refused yet. %>
        <% elsif !unchosen? %>
          <%# Nothing to name is nothing to click: requirement 27 makes the two
              names a condition of the request. What the directories answered is
              said in the card's own words — the code and the sentence they
              returned belong to the operator's console, not to a portal — and
              a directory that declined to answer is not a country publishing
              nothing, so the card says which of the two happened. %>
          <p class="fr-mb-0 requirement-card__refusal" lang="en" data-demo-card-announced>
            <%# The warning the pale red carries, said again in a sign: colour
                alone never carries information (RGAA 3.1). Hidden from the
                rendering the assistive technologies read, which has the
                sentence. %>
            <span class="fr-mr-1v" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span><%=
              if published_nothing?
                t('components.demo_requirement_card.no_provider_html', country: country_name)
              else
                t('components.demo_requirement_card.no_answer_html', country: country_name)
              end %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
